          %h2#valid_contexts Valid Contexts
          %p
            The above totality theorem is called “local” because it only says the interpretations are defined on the interpretation of the context; if the context is invalid then the latter interpretation could be empty. However, with the local totality theorem in hand, we can deduce a
            %em global
            totality theorem for valid contexts. Note that this parallels how the notion of valid context was defined after giving the inductive definition of the judgments, and also how the partial interpretation of contexts was defined after giving the partial interpretations of types and terms.
          %p The global totality theorem is:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is a valid context, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ \Gamma \⟧
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By induction on the length of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ () \⟧ = 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has a terminal object.
            %p
              For a context extension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,x:A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ \Gamma \⟧
              representable.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Initiality+Project+-+Partial+Interpretation"} Recall
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦\Gamma,x:A\⟧
              is defined as a pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo :
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Tm
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ty
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array { \⟦ \Gamma, x:A \⟧ &amp; \to &amp; Tm \\ \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\ U &amp; \to &amp; Ty. }
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tm
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ty
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tm\to Ty
              is, by our definition of CwF, a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+morphism"} representable morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a representable object.
            %p
              Now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is by definition the intersection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦\Gamma\⟧
              with the domain of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi A
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                        %mi type
                        %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ A \⟧^V_{type}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,x:A)
              is valid,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash A \, type
              is derivable, so by the local totality theorem, the domain of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi A
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                      %mi type
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ A \⟧^V_{type}
              %em contains
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦ \Gamma \⟧
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \⟦ \Gamma \⟧
          %p
            Furthermore, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tm
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ty
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tm\to Ty
            is
            %em algebraically
            represented, at each step we obtain a specified representing object for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \⟦\Gamma\⟧
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            also by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
